WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.319
In this walkthrough, we'll use the Higher Education template in a commercial Microsoft 365 tenant.

2
00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:15.348
The footage was recorded with release 3.8.21, while the commands and guidance are updated for release 3.8.24.

3
00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:19.842
We'll follow the same eight phases as the GCC Moderate guide.

4
00:00:20.892 --> 00:00:36.434
This is an unofficial demonstration: the footage uses public University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign pages inside a Microsoft lab tenant, so the tenant, account, and site names you see on screen are lab values, not values to copy.

5
00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:43.068
We'll verify the package, configure the settings, install the site, and review the result.

6
00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:49.210
Passing the automated checks is only part of deciding whether a deployment is ready for production.

7
00:00:49.939 --> 00:01:00.345
Download the release 3.8.24 implementation ZIP and its SHA256 receipt, not GitHub's automatically generated source archive.

8
00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:06.882
Run Get-FileHash on the ZIP and compare the result with the expected hash in the receipt.

9
00:01:06.882 --> 00:01:08.609
Continue only if they match.

10
00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:11.701
Use a new empty install folder.

11
00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:16.247
Copy the Org-Template content pack to a separate organization folder.

12
00:01:16.247 --> 00:01:22.441
Keep settings and records outside the extracted kit so a future release cannot overwrite them.

13
00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:29.399
Open the Deployment-Settings.json file in the organization folder, not the template inside the kit.

14
00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:37.351
Confirm the tenant, SharePoint hosts, unused group alias, and approved owner and reviewer accounts.

15
00:01:38.401 --> 00:01:41.716
Keep the Team private and external sharing disabled.

16
00:01:41.716 --> 00:01:44.775
Set the LearningEnvironment to Higher Education.

17
00:01:45.825 --> 00:01:50.641
If you're creating a new provisioning app, leave the PnP client ID blank.

18
00:01:50.641 --> 00:01:55.655
Don't copy another tenant's client ID or deployment report into this folder.

19
00:01:56.373 --> 00:01:58.661
Compare each setting with its source.

20
00:01:58.661 --> 00:02:08.243
Public policy links can be researched, but private mailboxes, ticket queues, incident routes, and tenant identities must come from the people who own them.

21
00:02:09.293 --> 00:02:11.864
Configure a monitored support mailbox.

22
00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:18.427
Then set the links for general support, technology requests, incident reporting, and AI guidance.

23
00:02:19.477 --> 00:02:22.251
Review the governance and training links as well.

24
00:02:23.301 --> 00:02:30.995
Keep lasting changes to generated page text in the organization's Content folder, and approved reference files in Assets.

25
00:02:31.713 --> 00:02:37.637
From the extracted kit folder, run the local content preflight against the organization folder.

26
00:02:37.637 --> 00:02:39.695
The commands are shown on screen.

27
00:02:40.745 --> 00:02:47.468
This checks the structured content before sign-in, including the calendar columns and required fields.

28
00:02:47.468 --> 00:02:53.071
It does not approve the links, tenant settings, policy wording, or reader experience.

29
00:02:54.121 --> 00:02:57.111
Fix every reported issue before continuing.

30
00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.710
Use PowerShell 7.4 or later with PnP PowerShell 3.2.0.

31
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:10.079
Script 01 always registers a new app for this organization profile.

32
00:03:10.079 --> 00:03:13.651
It is not a one-time, first-tenant-only step.

33
00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:22.859
Have an administrator authorized to grant consent run it, then confirm it saved a valid client ID before continuing.

34
00:03:23.909 --> 00:03:31.651
In Entra, confirm that all required delegated permissions are granted, and that Allow public client flows is set to Yes.

35
00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:45.027
Review the group naming policy, and check in the Teams admin center that the apps needed for the Website, PDF, PowerPoint, and SharePoint tabs are available to the installer and intended users.

36
00:03:45.744 --> 00:03:48.379
Run script 02 with SeedDemoContent.

37
00:03:48.379 --> 00:03:54.326
That switch loads the site's pages, catalogs, calendar, and governance content.

38
00:03:55.376 --> 00:04:02.446
Before creating resources, check the signed-in account, tenant, alias, owner, and target address.

39
00:04:03.496 --> 00:04:10.582
If the installer flags a naming policy issue, an unconfigured route, or a lab mailbox, stop and review it.

40
00:04:10.582 --> 00:04:15.462
Choosing Proceed is a documented pilot decision, not production approval.

41
00:04:16.512 --> 00:04:21.642
After installation, use the actual site address recorded in the deployment report.

42
00:04:21.642 --> 00:04:30.398
If an earlier attempt already created resources for the alias, follow the recovery procedure instead of starting another clean installation.

43
00:04:31.116 --> 00:04:38.034
Run the read-only checker with the organization folder, the actual site address, and the same ContentMode.

44
00:04:38.034 --> 00:04:40.970
Resolve every failure, and read each warning.

45
00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:47.574
Review Home, the tool pages, navigation, and catalog views as a regular reader.

46
00:04:47.574 --> 00:04:50.386
Follow the support and governance links.

47
00:04:51.436 --> 00:05:01.283
Confirm the Team is private, external sharing is disabled, no demo content remains, and each standard channel has exactly one correct welcome post.

48
00:05:01.283 --> 00:05:02.689
Check posts visually;

49
00:05:02.689 --> 00:05:06.306
the app can't read them back without extra permission.

50
00:05:07.356 --> 00:05:10.346
Keep the checker output and the manual review record.

51
00:05:11.064 --> 00:05:17.300
Publish reviewed changes from the organization folder with script 03 and interactive sign-in.

52
00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:22.262
Then run the same read-only checker and repeat the relevant manual review.

53
00:05:23.312 --> 00:05:26.673
Do not add RepairCapturedPages for a routine update;

54
00:05:26.673 --> 00:05:30.550
it can replace managed parts of Home and the captured pages.

55
00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:39.270
Complete the handoff only when both checker runs have passed and the required manual reviews are documented for this tenant.

56
00:05:39.999 --> 00:05:43.846
Passing the checker is not the same as production approval.

57
00:05:43.846 --> 00:05:50.693
The organization still needs to approve the content, security, accessibility, and operating arrangements.

58
00:05:51.743 --> 00:05:59.869
Keep the organization settings, deployment reports, run logs, both checker outputs, and manual review records together.

59
00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:07.845
For recovery or removal, use the administrator guide included with release 3.8.24.
